hydrasdr-host (1.1.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * libhydrasdr decimation stages (2x to 64x): fix the halfband ring
    buffers, 32 and 16 entries for 33 and 17 taps, whose batched stores
    overwrote the oldest history samples before the FIR read them. Every
    signal in a decimated band had images half (and, for int16 at 2x to
    8x, a quarter of) the output sample rate away, 43 to 57 dB below it.
    The stages now match a direct convolution bit-exactly.
  * Int16 stages: round the output shift instead of truncating it, which
    removes a DC line of 0.5 LSB per stage (-71 dBc at 64x for a -6 dBFS
    tone).
  * Int16 stages: unity gain per stage (output shift 15 on the Q15 taps)
    instead of 2x per stage. The int16 level at any decimation now
    matches 1x and float32; clients that compensated the old +6 dB per
    stage must drop that correction. Strong signals no longer clip at
    high decimation (the old chain clipped above -36 dBFS at 64x).

 -- Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@hydrasdr.com>  Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

hydrasdr-host (1.1.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Rename binary package libhydrasdr0 to libhydrasdr1 to match the
    shared library SONAME (libhydrasdr.so.1, SOVERSION=1 since v1.0.4).
    Fixes lintian package-name-doesnt-match-sonames warning.
  * Update libhydrasdr-dev and hydrasdr-host Depends accordingly.
  * Rename debian/libhydrasdr0.{install,dirs,udev} to libhydrasdr1.*
    and update debian/rules.

 -- Benjamin Vernoux <bvernoux@hydrasdr.com>  Sat, 02 May 2026 08:28:00 +0200

